- Each action is [dx, dy, dz, dyaw_deg]: translation in meters, yaw change in degrees.
- [dx, dy] is in the horizontal body frame of the PRECEDING pose: +dx forward, +dy right.
- Transform the translation with the preceding pose's yaw, then add dyaw_deg to get the
  next pose's yaw. Do not transform an action with the yaw it produces.
- Return relative increments, not absolute positions and not absolute yaw. Every value is
  a finite number.
- Keep each dyaw_deg within [-180, 180] degrees. A 180 degree turn keeps the requested
  direction: +180 and -180 rotate opposite ways.
